   "measured": "2026-11-06, issue #845 (PR #847 for processor pin 9210065779b0f698fd7bdb22323a1ed5b8482677, processor #212): RTL inputs at lane commit b16f0175ac402e124314a40d1ea9573e431684dc on dev 87e9d03aa2a4797957ac0124d0c7851a2eec234c, with FPGA-gPTP 135afd043309369a87ddbc8d6550aff8ec52a157; the lane's later commits change no synthesis input. Explicit synth.maxThreads 1, general.maxThreads 32; the recipe's three placement directives from one synthesis checkpoint, ExtraTimingOpt selected by the gate at WNS +0.373 ns over ExtraPostPlacementOpt +0.198 ns and AltSpreadLogic_high +0.047 ns. 15 of 15,850 slices remain. Maintainer decision: against the twelfth record the route moved by +517 LUT (tolerance +500), +875 FF (+600) and +55 slices (80), with RAMB36, RAMB18 and DSP unchanged, WNS -0.067 ns and WHS -0.024 ns; the gate refused the LUT and FF growth. The maintainer accepted this growth on 2026-11-06, with a re-baselined budget, in https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/845#issuecomment-6689114981. The differences include dev's movement since the twelfth record (8b76de69), which took FPGA-gPTP to 135afd04 and the processor to a9e84b66 without a new record. Every tolerance, floor and ceiling unchanged. docs/findings/234_PP_SHADOW_AREA_BASELINE.md retains the earlier records and this delta.",
